    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Peter I reigned from 1682 to 1725, sole ruler from 1696, and in 1721 took the title Emperor of All <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> after victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>.</li><li>He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-petersburg">Saint Petersburg</a> in 1703 and made it the capital, built a navy, and reorganised the state through the Governing Senate, the collegia, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/table-of-ranks">Table of Ranks</a> and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-synod">Holy Synod</a> that replaced the patriarchate.</li><li>His reforms were imposed by force: he crushed revolts such as the Streltsy and Bulavin rebellions, and historians still argue whether he set <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> on a modern course or, as Evgeny Anisimov put it, created an administrative command system.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boyar">Boyars</a> who wished to keep their beards after Peter's return from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-europe">Western Europe</a> had to pay an annual beard tax of one hundred rubles.</p></aside>
    </section>

